      "side": 1,
      "message": "[error] Line 744: 🔴 This positional mapping does not account for media entries that `Sdp::createOffer()` later drops when `enabled_` is false. After a rejected/disabled middle m-line, the old active SDP can have MIDs `[0,1,2]`, while the new offer list still has the disabled entry; this code assigns the later stream MID `2`, then `createOffer()` omits the middle entry and emits only MIDs `0` and `2`. The resulting BUNDLE group references a missing m-line (and changes the negotiated m-line layout), which a WebRTC peer can reject. Preserve/re-emit rejected m-lines with their original MIDs, or map MIDs using the post-filtered emitted indices; add a regression test for a disabled middle m-line.",
